# Mandatory access control with AppArmor.
#
# One package from Arch's own repositories, and the kernel side costs nothing:
# the stock Arch kernel is built with CONFIG_SECURITY_APPARMOR=y and
# CONFIG_SECURITY_APPARMOR_BOOTPARAM_VALUE=1, but CONFIG_LSM lists only
# "landlock,lockdown,yama,integrity,bpf", so AppArmor is compiled in and
# inactive until `lsm=` on the kernel command line names it. That is a one-line
# limine-entry-tool drop-in, which is what install/server/apparmor-server.sh
# writes. No kernel is rebuilt and no package is replaced.
#
# Mutually exclusive with the `selinux` addon: both are major LSMs and the
# kernel runs one of them at a time. The setup leaf refuses to install over the
# other one.
apparmor
